test: update tests that assumed ollama is always policy-blocked

The original PR #111 commit unblocked ollama when a known family model
is provided. Three pre-existing tests assumed ollama is hardcoded-blocked:

  - backend-readiness.test.js: 'keeps ollama probe details while still
    blocking launch under telemetry policy' — now expects the no-model
    'Ollama model is required' summary instead of the old hardcoded text.
  - spawner-telemetry-policy.test.js: 'blocks opaque backends' — uses
    'unobtanium-7b' (no family match) to keep exercising the blocked
    code path now that 'llama3.1:8b' (the spawner default) is allowed.
  - fleet-daemon.test.js: 'getStatus() exposes launchability and warns
    when a fleet has blocked backends' — model swapped from
    'qwen2.5-coder:7b' (now allowed) to 'unobtanium-7b' (still blocked)
    so the partial-launchable assertion holds.

48/48 in the three impacted suites; 60/60 in the policy + cost-tracker
suites added by this PR.


